  "title": "CHAPTER 9: EVOLUTION",
  "order": 9,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "e2q9mgv",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Introduction to Evolution"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Darwin's Theory of Evolution emphasizes Natural Selection and the Survival of the Fittest as primary mechanisms.",
        "Homologous organs share a common structural origin but serve different functions across different species.",
        "Analogous organs serve similar functions but differ in their fundamental anatomical structure and origin.",
        "Vestigial organs are non-functional remnants of structures that were functional in evolutionary ancestors.",
        "Mutations generate sudden, heritable variations that serve as essential raw materials for speciation."
      ],
      "id": "o4zcope"
    },
    {
      "type": "statStrip",
      "stats": [
        {
          "label": "Key Theories",
          "value": "Lamarckism & Darwinism",
          "icon": "book"
        },
