            "<p>Forelimbs of vertebrates</p>",
            "<p>Wings of bird &amp; insect</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "78fco18",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "13. Vestigial Organs"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "bymrzq8",
      "content": "Vestigial organs are reduced and functionless organs inherited from ancestors. Example: Appendix, wisdom teeth."
    },
    {
      "id": "oz1yxxk",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "14. Human Evolution"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "45l8gcs",
      "content": "Humans evolved from ape-like ancestors. Important stages include Australopithecus, Homo habilis, Homo erectus and Homo sapiens."
    },
    {
      "id": "ufmhzwa",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "15. Darwin vs Lamarck"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "c69pcgr",
      "content": "Jean Baptiste Lamarck proposed the Theory of Inheritance of Acquired Characters. He believed that traits acquired during an organism's lifetime are passed to offspring. Charles Darwin proposed the Theory of Natural Selection, stating that organisms with favorable variations survive and reproduce."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "xn0hndm",
      "content": "Modern genetics supports Darwin’s theory because acquired traits are not inherited genetically, whereas variations caused by genetic mutation are heritable."
    },
    {
