    {
      "id": "9dqrutt",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "17. Timeline of Human Evolution"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ljs5zet",
      "content": "Human evolution describes the gradual development of modern humans from ape-like ancestors. Fossil records and comparative anatomy provide evidence for human evolution."
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "RRB exams frequently test distinction between Homologous (same structure, different function) and Analogous (different structure, same function) organs.",
        "Lamarckism relies on 'Inheritance of Acquired Characters' whereas Darwinism is rooted in 'Natural Selection'.",
        "Commonly asked human vestigial organs include the vermiform appendix, wisdom teeth, and coccyx."
      ],
      "id": "pqwh5al"
    },
